WEBVTT

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:12.700
This is <i>Code Papillon</i>!

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.740
Midsummer's Knights, do you copy?

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:17.910
This is <i>Code Papillon</i>.

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:18.990
Do you copy?

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:23.500
This is Manatsu.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:24.920
Do you copy? Over.

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:30.210
Yes!

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:31.880
We've restored communication!

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.420
Is everyone all right, Captain?

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.140
We were ambushed by an unknown group.

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:38.220
They incapacitated the Nebula.

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:41.220
Teppei and Hana are okay, though.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:45.560
We're heading for Australian Central Command...

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:49.320
Might your attackers have been unmanned Globe weapons?

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:53.070
Salty Dog has a significant amount of influence in Australia.

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:55.110
I advise against contacting Central Command.

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:56.240
New plan, then.

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:57.780
I'm sending the data now.

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:01.910
To your north is the Carpentaria installation.

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:05.160
It's relatively undefended,

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:07.460
but it does house a newly deployed heavy transport craft.

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:09.170
The ground effect vehicle <i>Plavnik</i>.

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:12.510
If you're familiar with it, we can skip the instruction manual, Teppei.

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:14.010
I'll be fine.

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:16.970
I'll work my magic to get you the activation codes.

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:18.220
Hold it!

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:20.600
Doing something like that inside a Globe base

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:22.770
is only going to give them a valid reason to shoot you down!

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:24.680
The risk is too great!

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:27.900
Which is why...

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:32.570
I've hacked into ACC's primary mainframe and knocked it offline!

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:38.280
Wh-What?!

00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:41.660
I did not just hear what I think I heard.

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:43.790
I'm going to pretend I didn't.

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:45.540
Impressive.

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:48.500
And don't think I'm finished just yet!

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:51.460
If they're looking for a fight, they've found one!

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:54.010
I'm going to do everything I can to help you guys!

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:55.210
You're coming back alive!

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:56.630
Got it.

00:01:57.130 --> 00:02:01.640
Commander, the Midsummer's Knights will now begin their return trip to Tanegashima.

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:03.010
Roger that.

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:03.930
Be careful.

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:06.140
Thank you, Akari.

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:08.600
It's what I'm here for.

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:11.310
Your thanks fall on undeserved ears.

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:13.020
Listen, Akari...

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:16.650
Governor Yomatsuri told me—

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:17.900
Stop!

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:22.620
You can tell me when you get back.

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:25.080
Okay.

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:31.830
She's smiling a lot more often, lately.

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:36.550
What?

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:43.640
So it's you, eh?

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:51.850
Just be careful.

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:54.320
I'll be fine.

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:55.780
Everyone is with me.

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:00.860
It's thanks to Daichi and the others

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:03.160
that she can smile like that now, huh?

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:11.330
It's why I'm going to live in this town

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:18.510
I'm watching an endless dream

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:24.970
Aren't you watching too?

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:32.310
It's always close by no matter how far away it seems

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:39.150
Can't you see it too?

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:44.570
The things you can't normally say

00:03:44.570 --> 00:03:47.330
The things you try to express

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:49.830
The things you're willing to fight for

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:55.540
Standing on your own two feet

00:03:55.540 --> 00:04:02.220
The night sky illuminates them all

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:09.350
The first flash of lightning

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:15.690
This is our battle to fight

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:23.030
It's why I'm going to live in this town

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:31.500
This dream will absolutely come true

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:43.010
The commander will be heading over there—

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:51.180
Getting inside was child's play with their systems down.

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:53.020
Akari's amazing!

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:01.230
That's a magical girl for you.

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:12.200
What?

00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:15.040
Why is the <i>Plavnik</i> prepping for take-off?!

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:19.000
Let's go.

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:31.760
Australian Central Command and all of its peripheral bases

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:36.230
have lost primary mainframe connectivity for nearly an hour.

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:39.360
The computers are just now coming back online.

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:45.650
During the chaos they commandeered the ground effect vehicle <i>Plavnik</i>,

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:48.530
and are already en route to Tanegashima.

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:54.540
It will take about ninety minutes to get the Sarama Engine online.

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:57.460
Once it's operational,

00:05:57.460 --> 00:06:02.550
we will have the capability to intercept them before they reach Tanegashima.

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:05.670
Pillaging and running...

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:08.630
I feel kind of like a pirate.

00:06:09.140 --> 00:06:11.100
Pirate Captain Earth, eh?

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:12.930
Cut it out.

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:16.140
This is fun.

00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:24.280
Your Smile Means Everything

00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:25.280
Your Smile Means Everything

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:29.200
I must apologize, but I have business to attend to today.

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:32.120
You may leave tomorrow evening available, however.

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:35.330
Sorry, I'm busy tomorrow.

00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:37.500
Then perhaps the day after?

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:46.550
I'm sorry...

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:48.260
The day after won't work, either.

00:06:53.930 --> 00:06:55.390
So it's true.

00:06:55.390 --> 00:06:56.390
I've been dumped.

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:06.070
What are you doing?

00:07:06.530 --> 00:07:08.650
I'm done playing games.

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:11.610
I'm having Pac find us a place

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:16.080
where Lady Seiren can amass high-density libido for an all-out attack.

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:18.500
Hey...

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:22.630
Aren't you at all interested in this avatar's body?

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:24.460
No.

00:07:28.510 --> 00:07:30.630
You've got no libido...

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:33.840
This is bad.

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:38.560
They're going to pursue the three of them in the Sarama Engine.

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:40.430
The Sarama Engine?

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:41.270
Here it is.

00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:46.190
An unmanned Impactor developed primarily by the Ark Faction,

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:47.730
just like Cerberus.

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:51.450
It's much more mobile than its size would suggest.

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:55.410
It's also equipped with smaller attack units.

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:58.120
These specs are pretty impressive, actually.

00:07:58.660 --> 00:08:02.870
But once the <i>Plavnik</i> enters Japan's air defense zone,

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:06.040
they won't be able to touch it, will they?

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:07.090
I don't know.

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:10.670
I sincerely doubt that it will be that simple.

00:08:12.430 --> 00:08:16.470
We were right to send Salty Dog's observer back.

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:19.310
I had nothing to do with that.

00:08:19.720 --> 00:08:21.850
She probably thought that she'd be arrested

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:27.020
for trying to kidnap Mutou Hana if she stayed.

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:30.740
You're deploying the Sarama Engine?

00:08:31.070 --> 00:08:34.320
Won't that provoke the JSDF Air Force?

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:35.030
Over.

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:38.780
You needn't worry about that.

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:42.960
More importantly, appraise me of the situation at the Tanegashima base.

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:43.750
Over.

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:45.500
They're a tough nut to crack.

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:49.040
Groups composed of older people

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:52.380
tend to be experienced, knowledgeable, and careful,

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:56.050
but too cautious to make any serious moves.

00:08:56.800 --> 00:09:00.770
And groups composed of the young have an abundance of energy,

00:09:00.770 --> 00:09:04.230
but tend to lose control and destroy themselves.

00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:09.110
When the young and old work together with mutual respect, however,

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:11.570
they can forge an unwavering team.

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:15.650
Tanegashima has done that.

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:16.910
Over.

00:09:18.570 --> 00:09:19.870
Understood.

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:22.580
We would be wrong to underestimate them.

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:27.790
But we need Mutou Hana, no matter what.

00:09:27.790 --> 00:09:28.580
Over.

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:32.550
Even if we acquire Mutou Hana,

00:09:33.210 --> 00:09:36.800
there's no way she'll do as we command.

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:38.010
Over.

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:40.970
We'll cross that bridge when we come to it.

00:09:41.810 --> 00:09:44.850
She's still only a teenage girl.

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:48.650
They're willing to do anything it takes now.

00:09:55.900 --> 00:09:58.990
They need Hana that badly.

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:02.280
They need her power to operate the Blume.

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:08.870
Science Chief, thanks to your efforts,

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:11.210
we've not only learned where that spaceship came from,

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:14.420
but about the dangers our planet faces.

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:20.890
No, our technology couldn't even penetrate the ship's outer hull.

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:27.180
But fortunately, the entrainment analysis technology I developed allowed us

00:10:27.180 --> 00:10:31.860
to communicate with the intelligent life form inside.

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:34.070
That's all.

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:36.490
Science Chief,

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:41.950
is that young girl the intelligent life you've been communicating with?

00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:46.450
She looks like a girl... Is it her?

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:49.080
From my communications with her,

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:54.170
I had been led to believe that she was some kind of biological part of the spaceship.

00:10:54.710 --> 00:10:58.470
But since I've started speaking to her in person, it seems natural to me

00:10:58.470 --> 00:11:00.930
that the entity I've been conversing with is very much like a human girl...

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:05.310
No, that <i>is</i> a girl.

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:10.690
And she seems extremely afraid of returning to that spaceship.

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:17.690
Apparently, she can't leave it on her own.

00:11:18.440 --> 00:11:23.950
But, Science Chief... How was Manatsu Daichi alone

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:27.290
able to bring her out of the ship?

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:34.210
I've calculated the time when Sarama will reach the <i>Plavnik</i>.

00:11:34.750 --> 00:11:37.170
20:25 Japanese Standard Time!

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:40.470
You're coming home alive!

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:44.010
For the sake of this planet's future!

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:47.640
Now that I've gained a body,

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:50.020
I'm finding there are many things I didn't know.

00:11:50.730 --> 00:11:55.560
Peter Westvillage, Science Chief of Globe's Tanegashima base,

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:58.480
has sent an e-mail to Kube Masaki.

00:11:58.780 --> 00:12:01.030
Peter Westvillage...

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:06.240
For a short time, he was our company's science advisor.

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:11.160
Is he fishing for information about the Machine Goodfellows?

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:12.750
After the Kanda incident,

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:16.790
our company ostensibly has nothing to do with the Machine Goodfellows.

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:19.300
He won't find out about that.

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:20.590
No,

00:12:20.590 --> 00:12:26.550
he is asking for Kube Masaki's opinion on a scientific matter.

00:12:26.550 --> 00:12:28.680
What does he want to ask me about?

00:12:29.390 --> 00:12:32.640
Eternal life, apparently.

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:35.270
Oh, well isn't that interesting?

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:41.320
"If you attained eternal life, how might it alter your thought processes?"

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:43.740
But why me?

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:48.280
Macbeth currently possesses the world's most advanced machine intelligence.

00:12:48.280 --> 00:12:50.580
I'm of course referring to myself.

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:54.210
And Kube Masaki is the one man who interacts with me the most.

00:12:54.870 --> 00:12:57.500
Machine intelligence is fundamentally different from that of humanity.

00:12:57.500 --> 00:13:00.050
It is not fettered by a biological lifespan.

00:13:00.050 --> 00:13:03.340
It seems he wants to know

00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:09.180
how this machine intelligence regards its own existence, its eternal life.

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:12.350
Of course, if you have eternal life,

00:13:12.350 --> 00:13:16.650
the next thing you need is an infinite energy supply.

00:13:16.980 --> 00:13:21.690
The theory that the Livlasters were extradimensional life forms

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:23.190
that took the shape of a gun...

00:13:23.190 --> 00:13:27.490
Peter Westvillage was the one who originally wrote that report.

00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:31.540
If those guns have a will of their own,

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:36.000
Perhaps they are the ones trying to take over the galaxy...

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:39.750
My true enemies.

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:47.430
They're here.

00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:53.600
At this rate, they'll catch up to us.

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:10.870
We're always cutting it so close...

00:14:11.370 --> 00:14:13.370
There are only two kinds of "close."

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:16.710
"Close, but out" and "close, but safe."

00:14:17.410 --> 00:14:18.420
It's okay.

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:20.170
I'm sure we'll get home.

00:14:36.890 --> 00:14:39.190
It's not easy being a pirate, huh?

00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:47.070
In the distant past...

00:14:48.280 --> 00:14:53.080
Everything in my world was veiled in darkness.

00:14:54.580 --> 00:14:58.790
They created me to fire the Livlaster.

00:14:59.870 --> 00:15:03.630
But I couldn't do it.

00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:06.920
Darkness surrounded me on all sides,

00:15:07.460 --> 00:15:12.300
and the only thing they wanted me to do was to fire that gun.

00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:20.600
I wasn't even sure if I wanted to give them what they desired or not...

00:15:21.690 --> 00:15:26.020
But then, I thought I saw a light.

00:15:27.530 --> 00:15:32.950
It felt like someone's voice calling to me.

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:37.540
I knew that I needed to meet that person...

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:40.250
That I wanted to meet that person.

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:43.750
So I ran toward the light.

00:15:49.840 --> 00:15:50.840
And then...

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:53.340
I found you.

00:15:57.220 --> 00:15:58.810
Is it you?

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:04.770
No, that isn't it.

00:16:06.230 --> 00:16:08.730
You found me.

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:19.700
Hana?

00:16:20.660 --> 00:16:22.250
I'm going to the Flare Engine.

00:16:23.460 --> 00:16:24.120
You're going?

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:26.840
I'm going.

00:16:30.840 --> 00:16:32.050
I'm counting on you.

00:16:32.510 --> 00:16:33.050
Yeah.

00:16:34.340 --> 00:16:35.430
Let's do it.

00:16:39.390 --> 00:16:42.100
Both craft have entered Japan's air defense zone!

00:16:42.640 --> 00:16:44.390
Has the Japanese Air Force been scrambled?

00:16:44.390 --> 00:16:45.310
There's nothing to indicate that!

00:16:45.980 --> 00:16:49.020
Looks like Salty Dog is even pulling the strings here.

00:17:10.130 --> 00:17:10.710
Hana...

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:12.590
Commander,

00:17:13.260 --> 00:17:15.260
I'm beginning the mission.

00:17:15.930 --> 00:17:17.220
Mission?

00:17:17.220 --> 00:17:18.300
What mission?

00:17:22.270 --> 00:17:24.940
That is the full story behind Operation Summer.

00:17:25.810 --> 00:17:27.440
I'll ask you straight out.

00:17:28.020 --> 00:17:29.150
Mutou Hana,

00:17:29.940 --> 00:17:35.240
do you have the skills to complete this mission, and the will to see it through?

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:46.460
I'm okay now.

00:17:58.760 --> 00:18:01.180
I have no idea how we're able to keep doing this...

00:18:04.470 --> 00:18:06.940
It's too big for us to damage!

00:18:07.640 --> 00:18:09.600
It's overwhelming them.

00:18:10.360 --> 00:18:12.860
Capture Mutou Hana!

00:18:31.170 --> 00:18:33.170
Is this some kind of nasty dog-monster?

00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:41.300
Hana!

00:18:47.980 --> 00:18:50.690
I'll deploy a team to locate Mutou Hana.

00:18:51.310 --> 00:18:54.650
Eliminate Manatsu Daichi and Arashi Teppei.

00:18:55.230 --> 00:18:59.240
Crush the Intercept Faction's hopes!

00:19:03.620 --> 00:19:05.990
High energy readings from under the nearby sea!

00:19:08.660 --> 00:19:10.250
It's surfacing.

00:19:10.250 --> 00:19:11.580
Could this be...

00:19:15.670 --> 00:19:17.550
Get them, Hana!

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:53.420
The <i>Blume</i> surfaced?

00:19:54.710 --> 00:19:57.380
Is Mutou Hana operating it?

00:19:59.090 --> 00:20:00.470
Don't!

00:20:00.470 --> 00:20:03.220
Why would you damage the <i>Blume</i>?!

00:20:55.940 --> 00:20:57.270
It's huge.

00:20:58.110 --> 00:20:59.980
That's the <i>Blume</i>?

00:21:03.900 --> 00:21:06.660
I'm okay now.

00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:11.660
If you enter the <i>Blume</i>, you won't be able to leave by your own will.

00:21:12.250 --> 00:21:13.160
Right?

00:21:14.290 --> 00:21:15.370
It's okay.

00:21:15.960 --> 00:21:18.290
The captain will come for me.

00:21:18.290 --> 00:21:20.300
I will, no matter what.

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:22.130
So it's okay.

00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:27.260
Then only Manatsu Daichi can bring you out of the <i>Blume</i>.

00:21:27.260 --> 00:21:29.390
That's right, isn't it?

00:21:30.390 --> 00:21:31.310
In other words...

00:21:32.390 --> 00:21:34.350
If anything happens to him,

00:21:34.350 --> 00:21:37.690
we'll lose the ability to extricate you from that ship.

00:21:37.690 --> 00:21:39.860
Do you realize this?

00:21:40.770 --> 00:21:42.230
I do.

00:21:44.780 --> 00:21:46.200
And you're all right with that?

00:21:47.110 --> 00:21:47.820
Yes.

00:21:48.740 --> 00:21:51.580
If I lose the captain,

00:21:52.740 --> 00:21:54.830
there'll be no point in leaving the ship anyway.

00:21:56.920 --> 00:21:57.620
Hana...

00:24:13.010 --> 00:24:15.220
The spaceship <i>Blume</i> goes up to the orbiting satellite

00:24:15.220 --> 00:24:16.600
to rendezvous with the <i>Tenkaido</i>.

00:24:17.180 --> 00:24:20.890
